                <pb facs="0754" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg660"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 302.—Clipping from Japan Daily
                        Mail.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The Keizai Zasshi publishes a note in which it points out that, while Japan and
                    the United States of America are such near neighbors, geographically, the actual
                    commercial routes are unnecessarily long, the commodities passing between the
                    two countries being mostly carried by way of the Suez Canal. Our contemporary
                    recommends the Nippon Yusen Kaisha to open communication on the Pacific between
                    this Country and America.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
